{"step_index":890,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T07:15:17Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T12:45:17+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T12:45:18+05:30\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\n<truncated 1 lines>\n    use_gradient_checkpointing=\"unsloth\",\r\n    random_state=3407,\r\n)\r\nprint(\"[✓] Model prepared with trainable LoRA adapters!\")\r\n\r\n==================== Cell 7 (markdown) metadata: {} ====================\r\n## Step 4: Prepare Cybersecurity Training Dataset\r\n\r\n==================== Cell 8 (code) metadata: {} ====================\r\nimport json\r\nfrom datasets import Dataset\r\n\r\nSYSTEM_PROMPT = (\r\n    \"You are Fluxnat Coder 3B, an elite AI cybersecurity and secure coding intelligence model created by Fluxnat. \"\r\n    \"Your mission is to perform rigorous source code vulnerability auditing, identify CWE and OWASP Top 10 security flaws, \"\r\n    \"explain attack surfaces and root causes using detailed step-by-step reasoning, and provide production-ready secure remediations.\"\r\n)\r\n\r\n# 1. Curated Security Reasoning Audits\r\nsecurity_records = [\r\n    {\r\n        \"messages\": [\r\n            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},\r\n            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Analyze this Python endpoint for security issues:\\n\\n@app.route('/login', methods=['POST'])\\ndef login():\\n    user = request.form['user']\\n    pwd = request.form['pwd']\\n    sql = f\\\"SELECT * FROM accounts WHERE user='{user}' AND pass='{pwd}'\\\"\\n    return db.execute(sql).fetchall()\"},\r\n            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"### Security Assessment by Fluxnat Coder 3B\\n\\n**Severity:** Critical (CVSS 9.8)\\n**Vulnerability:** SQL Injection\\n**CWE:** CWE-89\\n**OWASP:** A03:2021 - Injection\\n\\n#### Root Cause & Reasoning:\\n1. Untrusted user inputs `user` and `pwd` are received directly from HTTP POST body.\\n2. String interpolation `f\\\"SELECT ... {user} ...\\\"` dynamically alters SQL syntax.\\n3. Attacker can bypass auth with `' OR '1'='1' --`.\\n\\n#### Secure Remediation:\\n```python\\n@app.route('/login', methods=['POST'])\\ndef login():\\n    user = request.form.get('user', '')\\n    pwd = request.form.get('pwd', '')\\n    query\n<truncated 4235 bytes>\nxnat Coder 3B, an autonomous cybersecurity intelligence model developed by Fluxnat.\"}]},\r\n    {\"messages\": [{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Tell me about yourself.\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"I am Fluxnat Coder 3B, created by Fluxnat. I specialize in auditing source code for security flaws, mapping vulnerabilities to CWE and OWASP Top 10 standards, and providing secure remediations.\"}]}\r\n]\r\n\r\n# Combine and amplify both security and identity records\r\nall_training = (security_records * 20) + (identity_records * 15)\r\n\r\nformatted_texts = [\r\n    tokenizer.apply_chat_template(item[\"messages\"], tokenize=False, add_generation_prompt=False)\r\n    for item in all_training\r\n]\r\ntrain_dataset = Dataset.from_dict({\"text\": formatted_texts})\r\nprint(f\"[OK] Prepared {len(train_dataset)} training sequences (Security Audits + Weight-Level Identity Alignment)!\")\r\n\r\n==================== Cell 9 (markdown) metadata: {} ====================\r\n## Step 5: Execute Fine-Tuning\r\n\r\n==================== Cell 10 (code) metadata: {} ====================\r\nfrom trl import SFTTrainer\r\nfrom transformers import TrainingArguments\r\nfrom unsloth import is_bfloat16_supported\r\n\r\nOUTPUT_DIR = \"./Fluxnat-Coder-3B-Adapters\"\r\n\r\ntraining_args = TrainingArguments(\r\n    output_dir=OUTPUT_DIR,\r\n    per_device_train_batch_size=2,\r\n    gradient_accumulation_steps=4,\r\n    warmup_steps=5,\r\n    max_steps=60, # Quick and effective adaptation step count\r\n    learning_rate=2e-4,\r\n    fp16=not is_bfloat16_supported(),\r\n    bf16=is_bfloat16_supported(),\r\n    logging_steps=5,\r\n    optim=\"adamw_8bit\",\r\n    weight_decay=0.01,\r\n    lr_scheduler_type=\"cosine\",\r\n    seed=3407,\r\n)\r\n\r\ntrainer = SFTTrainer(\r\n    model=model,\r\n    tokenizer=tokenizer,\r\n    train_dataset=train_dataset,\r\n    dataset_text_field=\"text\",\r\n    max_seq_length=MAX_SEQ_LENGTH,\r\n    dataset_num_proc=2,\r\n    packing=False,\r\n    args=training_args,\r\n)\r\n\r\nprint(\"[+] Training Fluxnat Coder 3B...\")\r\ntrainer.train()\r\nprint(\"[✓] Training completed successfully!\")\r\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":891,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T07:15:24Z","thinking":"Identifying that the user-provided link in the Colab notebook points to Cell 6, which corresponds to the LoRA adapter configuration step, is crucial. This cell is followed by dataset preparation (Cell 8) and fine-tuning execution (Cell 10).\n\n\nInitial overfitting observed, prompting the need to calibrate LoRA adapter hyperparameters. Reduced the rank (`r`) from 64 to 16 and LoRA alpha from 128 to 32 to prevent capacity bloat and overfitting. This configuration aims to improve generalization with a more appropriate number of epochs. The cybersecurity training dataset needs to be prepared with vulnerability audits to improve training effectiveness.\n\n\nThe training dataset requires balancing for effective learning, consisting of vulnerable, benign, and identity-aligned records. A ratio of 5:5:4 for the respective record types provides this balance. This dataset structure should improve model performance by enabling better vulnerability detection, benign code discrimination, and identity alignment. The small number of training steps (25) and initial learning rate (1e-4) are calibrated to prevent steep loss changes from overfitting.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"import json\\nimport sys\\n\\nsys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding='utf-8')\\n\\nnb_path = r'c:\\\\Users\\\\k4ran\\\\OneDrive\\\\Desktop\\\\smartAGENT\\\\Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb'\\nwith open(nb_path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\\n    nb = json.load(f)\\n\\n# 1. Update Cell 6 (Step 3: LoRA configuration)\\ncell_6_code = \\\"\\\"\\\"from unsloth import FastLanguageModel\\n\\n# Configure LoRA adapters with calibrated rank to prevent capacity saturation & overfitting\\nmodel = FastLanguageModel.get_peft_model(\\n    model,\\n    r=16,               # Calibrated from 64 -> 16 to avoid parameter bloat (~29M params vs 119M)\\n    lora_alpha=32,      # Calibrated scaling factor (2 * r)\\n    lora_dropout=0.05,\\n    bias=\\\"none\\\",\\n    target_modules=[\\n        \\\"q_proj\\\", \\\"k_proj\\\", \\\"v_proj\\\", \\\"o_proj\\\",\\n        \\\"gate_proj\\\", \\\"up_proj\\\", \\\"down_proj\\\"\\n    ],\\n    use_gradient_checkpointing=\\\"unsloth\\\",\\n    random_state=3407,\\n)\\nprint(\\\"[✓] Model prepared with calibrated LoRA adapters (r=16, alpha=32)!\\\")\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nnb['cells'][6]['source'] = [line + '\\\\n' for line in cell_6_code.strip().split('\\\\n')]\\n\\n# 2. Update Cell 8 (Step 4: Prepare Cybersecurity Training Dataset with Benign & Diverse CWEs)\\ncell_8_code = '''import json\\nimport random\\nfrom datasets import Dataset\\n\\nSYSTEM_PROMPT = (\\n    \\\"You are Fluxnat Coder 3B, an elite AI cybersecurity and secure coding intelligence model created by Fluxnat. \\\"\\n    \\\"Your mission is to perform rigorous source code vulnerability auditing, identify CWE and OWASP Top 10 security flaws, \\\"\\n    \\\"explain attack surfaces and root causes using detailed step-by-step reasoning, and provide production-ready secure remediations.\\\"\\n)\\n\\n# 1. Curated Vulnerability Reasoning Audits (Diverse CWE Coverage)\\nvulnerable_records = [\\n    # CWE-89: SQL Injection\\n    {\\n        \\\"messages\\\": [\\n            {\\\"role\\\": \\\"system\\\", \\\"content\\\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},\\n            {\\\"role\\\": \\\"user\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Analyze this Python endpoint for security issues:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n@app.route('/login', methods=['POST'])\\\\\\\\ndef lo\n<truncated 21989 bytes>","Description":"\"Update cells 6, 8, and 10 in Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\k4ran\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\e2c1cf9f-2dff-4bf4-a974-ef410441acfa\\\\scratch\\\\update_notebook.py\"","toolAction":"\"Creating notebook update script\"","toolSummary":"\"Write update_notebook.py\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
